{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "GLM-5.2", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:34 — Minor: The IPv4 loopback (0.0.0.0) is blocked, but IPv6 loopback (::0) and unspecified (::) are not explicitly blocked in isPrivateOrBlockedIp, potentially allowing bypass in environments mapping unspecified addresses.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:124-128 — Correctness/SSRF: The destination is resolved to an IPv4 address before validating it against the allowlist. If \"mud.revivalworld.org\" (or a local dev host) resolves to IPv6, this will fail with a \"dns failed\" error.\n- apps/web/src/App.tsx:46-54 — Correctness: The user can configure any arbitrary host and port in the web UI. While the proxy correctly blocks these in prod mode via assertDestinationAllowed, the browser will just fail to connect silently. Consider limiting the UI options for production builds.\n- packages/protocol/src/telnet.ts:101-107 — Correctness: TelnetParser will crash on a malformed subnegotiation (IAC SB <option> <no IAC SE>). It loops j to the end and slices payload without verifying j+1 is IAC.\n- packages/vt/src/sgr.ts:111-114 — Correctness: tokenizeAnsi includes a regex range of [ -/], which incorrectly matches final bytes (like @) when combined with the second [@-~] range, consuming characters.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-HYPxwB", "error": null }
